WEBVTT

00:04.054 --> 00:06.579
Aren't you gonna wash your hands
before you eat?

00:06.756 --> 00:09.520
No, I wrap the toilet paper on my fingers
like an oven mitt.

00:11.394 --> 00:12.986
You could catch a puck with it.

00:13.997 --> 00:16.261
So, Mom, what brings you
to our neck of the woods?

00:16.433 --> 00:19.766
I'm showing a house down the beach,
thought I'd swing by and see my grandson.

00:19.936 --> 00:21.267
Ta-da!

00:26.009 --> 00:28.273
- Nice house?
- Oh, magnificent.

00:28.445 --> 00:32.541
Priced to move. The owner lost everything
in the stock market, killed himself.

00:32.716 --> 00:35.708
- Oh, that's terrible.
- He didn't do it in the house. Thank God.

00:36.453 --> 00:40.890
Even with an ocean view,
suicide homes are a bitch to unload.

00:42.358 --> 00:45.122
Keep that in mind
you wanna teach your brother a lesson.

00:46.362 --> 00:47.852
Thanks for the tip.

00:48.932 --> 00:50.365
Good morning, Alan.

00:50.533 --> 00:51.761
Morning, Jake.

00:51.935 --> 00:53.664
Satan.

00:56.806 --> 00:58.398
Good morning, darling.

00:58.575 --> 00:59.701
Two coffee cups?

01:00.276 --> 01:03.074
- Did you have a friend spend the night?
- Yes, I did.

01:03.246 --> 01:05.737
Couldn't get her to stand on the trap door,
huh?

01:06.950 --> 01:09.384
Charlie, I don't have time for coffee,
so...

01:10.787 --> 01:13.278
- Oh. Hello.
- Hello.

01:13.456 --> 01:16.357
Uh, Chelsea, this is my mother.
Mom, this is Chelsea.

01:16.526 --> 01:17.584
Nice to meet you.

01:17.761 --> 01:19.319
Nice to meet you too.

01:19.496 --> 01:20.758
Welcome back to the States.

01:23.666 --> 01:24.690
Thank you.

01:24.868 --> 01:26.426
Where have I been?

01:26.603 --> 01:28.901
Charlie says you have a place in Italy-

01:29.072 --> 01:33.372
You know, Chelsea. Sometimes
when I'm drunk, I make up stories, so...

01:33.676 --> 01:35.906
You know, grain of salt.

01:36.212 --> 01:39.045
That is quite an engagement ring.

01:39.215 --> 01:40.375
Thank you.

01:40.550 --> 01:42.677
Does your fiancé know about this one?

01:43.219 --> 01:45.084
My fiancé is this one.

01:51.294 --> 01:53.125
You want me put this in a travel mug?

01:54.397 --> 01:56.297
You didn't tell your mother
we're engaged?

01:56.466 --> 01:59.697
If she hadn't sold me the house,
she wouldn't even know where I live.

02:07.210 --> 02:09.974
When were you gonna tell her about me?
At the wedding?

02:10.146 --> 02:13.604
Well, technically,
I think we have up to a year after that.

02:13.783 --> 02:16.081
Shame on you. I am so sorry.

02:16.252 --> 02:18.584
It's all right, dear. I'm used to it.

02:19.088 --> 02:21.147
Although a phone call
would have been nice.

02:23.359 --> 02:25.452
It's good to meet you. Excuse me.

02:32.902 --> 02:35.564
So yea or nay on the travel mug?

02:36.105 --> 02:37.902
Charlie, you broke
your mother's heart.

02:48.785 --> 02:50.480
How is that funny?

02:50.653 --> 02:52.245
It's not. Guys, a little respect.

02:54.357 --> 02:55.654
What is wrong with you?

02:57.060 --> 02:59.255
Same stuff as always, nothing new.

02:59.829 --> 03:02.821
Does this smell like butt to you?

03:12.742 --> 03:14.300
CHARLIE:
I'm glad you came over.

03:14.711 --> 03:16.178
That was the plan, wasn't it?

03:17.747 --> 03:20.181
Yeah, but I thought you might
still be angry with me.

03:20.350 --> 03:23.251
I'm not angry, Charlie.
I'm just disappointed.

03:23.853 --> 03:26.720
Gee, I'd kind of prefer it
if you were angry.

03:27.457 --> 03:29.015
Why?

03:29.459 --> 03:31.825
Because angry sex is hot.

03:31.995 --> 03:34.862
Disappointed sex is-
Well, we might as well be married.

03:36.532 --> 03:37.590
Just brush your teeth.

03:37.767 --> 03:39.667
Brushing.

03:40.203 --> 03:43.502
Look, I understand you have
a difficult relationship with your mom.

03:43.673 --> 03:44.833
Uh-huh.

03:45.008 --> 03:46.908
But it make things kind of tough on me.

03:47.510 --> 03:49.910
Hey, I don't expect you to dislike her
right away.

03:50.079 --> 03:53.048
Give it time, let it happen naturally.

03:54.517 --> 03:55.814
That's not funny.

03:55.985 --> 03:59.751
If I'm gonna marry into your family,
I want us to act like a family.

03:59.923 --> 04:01.083
Care for each other.

04:01.257 --> 04:04.226
With my family, it's kind of either-or.

04:04.560 --> 04:05.618
Let me put it this way.

04:05.795 --> 04:07.786
I'm taking your mother
to lunch on Thursday.

04:12.702 --> 04:14.135
You're doing what?

04:14.637 --> 04:17.902
I'm not going to participate
in this childish little feud of yours.

04:18.708 --> 04:20.471
It's not a childish feud.

04:21.077 --> 04:22.977
Boy.

04:23.513 --> 04:27.574
What's wrong with me having a warm
and healthy relationship with your mother?

04:27.750 --> 04:30.651
Well, for starters, you'll be the only one.

04:31.955 --> 04:34.014
Ever.

04:34.724 --> 04:36.248
Oh, don't be so dramatic.

04:36.426 --> 04:38.951
No, no. No. No.
I'm not being dramatic enough.

04:39.128 --> 04:41.289
I should be wearing tights
and holding a skull.

04:42.899 --> 04:46.062
- Preferably hers.
- It's just lunch.

04:46.235 --> 04:49.068
That's what Hitler said
to Czechoslovakia.

04:49.906 --> 04:52.238
Hitler said "It's just lunch?"

04:52.408 --> 04:54.501
Well, he said it in German.

04:54.677 --> 04:56.508
Watch the History Channel.

04:57.981 --> 04:59.846
Charlie, I'm not doing this to hurt you.

05:00.917 --> 05:04.978
By my spending time with your mother
I can get a better understanding of you.

05:05.722 --> 05:07.417
Chelsea, trust me.

05:07.590 --> 05:10.286
Any insight you gain into me
via my mother...

05:10.460 --> 05:14.419
...will end our relationship faster than
catching me in bed with a farm animal.

05:16.399 --> 05:18.424
Just relax. It'll be fine.

05:19.035 --> 05:21.469
That's what Hitler said to Poland.

05:23.873 --> 05:25.101
And for the record...

05:25.274 --> 05:28.209
...as long as we've been going out,
I've never met your mother.

05:28.378 --> 05:29.640
My mother's in Illinois.

05:29.812 --> 05:32.872
Oh, yeah, and my mother's in "Italy."

05:33.683 --> 05:36.049
My mother really lives in Illinois.

05:36.219 --> 05:38.187
And besides, when you meet her...

05:38.354 --> 05:41.221
...you will count your blessings
you have your mom.

05:42.058 --> 05:45.494
Tell you what, I'll trade you,
sight unseen, my mom for yours.

05:45.661 --> 05:49.062
- Charlie-
- I'll throw in Alan and a couple of steaks.

05:50.400 --> 05:51.731
Come here.

05:51.901 --> 05:53.630
No. I don't wanna.

05:54.804 --> 05:56.669
I'm too upset.

05:57.640 --> 05:59.471
Okay. Good night.

06:00.810 --> 06:04.871
I'm sorry, I can't separate my emotions
from my body.

06:05.048 --> 06:06.072
I understand.

06:06.249 --> 06:09.184
I don't wanna punish you.
If my heart's not in it...

06:09.352 --> 06:11.912
...then it's just my penis
going through the motions.

06:12.789 --> 06:15.019
Well, we certainly wouldn't want that.

06:15.191 --> 06:16.749
Good night.

06:16.926 --> 06:18.689
Good night.

06:33.976 --> 06:35.568
Chelsea.

06:35.745 --> 06:38.339
I'm not upset anymore.

06:40.817 --> 06:42.808
Charlie, I'm sleeping.

06:42.985 --> 06:44.418
I know.

06:44.587 --> 06:48.318
Can you just wake up enough
so it's not weird?

06:51.227 --> 06:53.593
Never mind. Sweet dreams.

06:58.067 --> 06:59.762
Okay, let me remind you...

06:59.936 --> 07:03.099
...this is Malibu beachfront property.

07:03.272 --> 07:06.207
The previous owner
had a spectacular view...

07:06.375 --> 07:10.106
...as he filled his pockets with rocks
and jumped into the pool.

07:12.148 --> 07:14.275
- Mom?
- Hang on.

07:14.851 --> 07:17.877
No, it's not a suicide home.

07:18.387 --> 07:22.289
At most, it's suicide adjacent.

07:23.126 --> 07:26.152
All right, get back to me.

07:26.729 --> 07:27.821
What are you doing here?

07:28.898 --> 07:31.230
What, I can't come visit
my mother at work?

07:31.400 --> 07:36.235
Well, I suppose you could, but I've been
here for 22 years, and you never have.

07:36.405 --> 07:38.771
Well, maybe if you validated parking...

07:40.910 --> 07:42.901
Or any part of my life.

07:43.079 --> 07:44.478
What do you want, Charlie?

07:45.047 --> 07:49.211
Okay, first of all, I wanna apologize
for not telling you about Chelsea...

07:49.385 --> 07:50.545
...and the engagement.

07:50.720 --> 07:52.915
I know that was wrong
and selfish of me.

07:54.090 --> 07:55.114
Thank you.

07:55.291 --> 07:57.987
Good.
I'm glad we got that out of the way.

07:58.161 --> 08:01.028
So I understand
you guys are having lunch tomorrow.

08:01.197 --> 08:02.926
Yes, we are. Is that a problem?

08:03.099 --> 08:04.691
No, no. No, it's great.

08:04.867 --> 08:08.462
I came all the way here and paid for
my own parking to tell you it's great.

08:09.305 --> 08:10.636
Uh-huh.

08:11.774 --> 08:12.798
All right.

08:12.975 --> 08:14.943
Let's put our cards on the table.

08:15.111 --> 08:16.135
What's your angle?

08:17.213 --> 08:18.271
Angle?

08:18.447 --> 08:19.675
I have no angle.

08:19.849 --> 08:22.181
Yeah, and I have no hangover.

08:22.785 --> 08:26.152
Look, Charlie.
If you're really gonna marry this woman...

08:26.322 --> 08:28.381
...I wanna get started on the right foot.

08:28.558 --> 08:31.459
I don't wanna make the mistake
I made with Alan's wife, June.

08:31.627 --> 08:34.653
- Judith.
- Oh, whatever.

08:35.398 --> 08:37.491
Heinous woman.

08:38.100 --> 08:40.500
The fact remains, had I overlooked that...

08:40.670 --> 08:43.935
...and welcomed her,
she wouldn't have kept me at arms length...

08:44.106 --> 08:48.008
...during Jake's formative years,
and I'd have a better relationship with him.

08:48.177 --> 08:52.807
- You want a better relationship with him?
- Not the way he is now.

08:54.083 --> 08:55.812
But if I'd gotten to him earlier...

08:55.985 --> 08:58.510
...he wouldn't have the manners
of an outhouse rat.

09:00.223 --> 09:04.182
So bottom line, you want a good
relationship with Chelsea...

09:04.360 --> 09:06.692
...so you get your hooks
into the next generation?

09:07.230 --> 09:10.529
Can't I just wanna be a loving mother
and grandmother?

09:11.267 --> 09:15.931
Well, I suppose you could, but I've been
here 40 years, and you never have.

09:19.642 --> 09:21.109
Evelyn Harper.

09:21.811 --> 09:24.371
Oh. Hello, Dr. Yakimura. What's up?

09:25.281 --> 09:28.842
Oh, that is good news.
What's the address?

09:30.953 --> 09:33.421
Nice neighborhood. Thanks for the tip.

09:35.458 --> 09:36.516
What's the good news?

09:36.692 --> 09:38.182
Massive coronary in Brentwood.

09:39.895 --> 09:41.385
Six bedrooms, four baths...

09:41.564 --> 09:45.125
...and a fully-equipped gym
the fat idiot shouldn't have been using.

09:46.702 --> 09:47.726
Excuse me.

09:47.903 --> 09:51.600
Mommy has to fly faster
than the other vultures.

10:18.901 --> 10:22.564
Your mother took me
to the most adorable little restaurant.

10:23.072 --> 10:24.903
No kidding.

10:25.074 --> 10:28.339
It's called Mon Grenier Du Vivre.
You know what that means?

10:29.278 --> 10:32.213
Probably "The Spider's Web."

10:32.381 --> 10:33.678
Charlie.

10:33.849 --> 10:35.840
"The Devil's Barbecue"?

10:36.919 --> 10:37.943
Be nice.

10:38.287 --> 10:39.311
Sorry.

10:42.191 --> 10:44.421
"Bitch in the Box."

10:47.563 --> 10:51.021
- So, what did you guys talk about?
- You know, everything.

10:51.200 --> 10:53.498
She's so smart and funny.

10:53.669 --> 10:56.331
She's been through so much.
She's a real survivor.

10:56.505 --> 11:01.272
Just remember, in order for her
to be a survivor, others had to die.

11:01.444 --> 11:02.934
Okay, that's enough.

11:03.112 --> 11:04.841
Your mom's a terrific lady.

11:05.014 --> 11:07.482
I'm starting to think
any problem you have with her...

11:07.650 --> 11:09.675
...is your problem, not hers.

11:09.852 --> 11:11.911
Oh, damn, it's too late.

11:12.088 --> 11:13.783
You're infected with the virus.

11:14.790 --> 11:16.223
Stop it.

11:16.392 --> 11:20.453
I'm sorry, but when you fall asleep tonight,
I'm gonna have to set you on fire.

11:21.163 --> 11:22.289
Shut up.

11:22.465 --> 11:26.993
Believe me, when you meet my mom,
you'll thank God for Evelyn.

11:27.169 --> 11:28.534
What the hell is your mom...

11:28.704 --> 11:31.798
...a rabid werewolf
that craps hot lava on people?

11:32.908 --> 11:34.671
Never mind about my mother.

11:34.844 --> 11:35.868
Let's play.

11:36.746 --> 11:37.838
I don't know.

11:38.647 --> 11:39.875
What's the matter?

11:40.516 --> 11:42.984
All this talk about mothers,
I'm not in the mood.

11:43.152 --> 11:44.676
Bet I could get you in the mood.

11:45.321 --> 11:48.848
Maybe, but it would be
a cheap manipulation.

11:50.292 --> 11:53.489
All right, but don't come
rubbing up against me in the night.

11:53.996 --> 11:55.224
I won't.

11:55.398 --> 11:57.025
Fine. Good night.

11:57.199 --> 11:58.996
Good night.

12:12.281 --> 12:14.772
Don't even think about it.

12:23.159 --> 12:25.184
Listen, you gotta do me a favor.

12:25.361 --> 12:27.329
That's what I live for.

12:27.763 --> 12:29.993
Sarcasm is for winners, Alan.

12:34.703 --> 12:35.727
What can I do for you?

12:36.238 --> 12:41.904
Chelsea's somehow gotten it into her head
that mom is, you know, human.

12:43.512 --> 12:44.843
You need to set her straight.

12:45.014 --> 12:47.983
- Why don't you set her straight?
- She doesn't believe me.

12:48.150 --> 12:50.675
Probably because I turned out okay.

12:53.055 --> 12:56.513
She needs to hear from somebody
whose life is wrecked and unsalvageable.

12:56.692 --> 12:57.989
I.e., you.

12:59.528 --> 13:01.928
Thanks.
And what do you expect me to say?

13:03.365 --> 13:06.596
I don't know, just tell her
about your phobias, your obsessions...

13:06.769 --> 13:10.728
...your failures: work, marriage,
and parenthood. She'll connect the dots.

13:12.141 --> 13:13.665
You know what? I think I'll pass.

13:14.210 --> 13:17.373
Oh, come on.
I always back you up when you need me.

13:18.047 --> 13:19.674
When have you ever backed me up?

13:21.317 --> 13:23.285
Okay,
let's stay focused on my problems.

13:24.553 --> 13:27.249
I'm not gonna argue
we didn't have a difficult childhood...

13:27.423 --> 13:29.118
...but really, who had a good one?

13:29.291 --> 13:31.054
Isn't it time we forgive and forget?

13:32.394 --> 13:33.554
Where's this coming from?

13:33.729 --> 13:36.527
No, I'm just saying
that maybe our lives would be richer...

13:36.699 --> 13:40.066
...if we let go of this pointless resentment
toward our mother...

13:40.236 --> 13:42.602
...and just move on with our lives.

13:43.072 --> 13:45.063
She got to you, didn't she?

13:45.774 --> 13:48.436
- What are you talking about?
- What did she do?

13:48.611 --> 13:49.635
Pay off your car?

13:51.113 --> 13:53.240
Get that dead black tooth fixed?

13:54.216 --> 13:56.377
Listen to yourself.
I have to go to work.

13:57.319 --> 13:59.719
- Hold it.
- What?

14:00.189 --> 14:02.419
- Your watch.
- What about it?

14:02.591 --> 14:05.492
It doesn't have Hamburglars
on the wrist band.

14:08.163 --> 14:09.562
So?

14:09.732 --> 14:12.257
- Let me see it.
- No, it's mine.

14:12.835 --> 14:14.496
CHARLIE:
Let me see it.

14:14.670 --> 14:16.433
Let me see it.

14:18.474 --> 14:19.839
This is a Rolex.

14:20.809 --> 14:22.333
You sold me out for a watch.

14:22.511 --> 14:24.877
Hey, I did not sell you out for a watch.

14:25.047 --> 14:27.106
I sold you out
for a Swiss chronometer.

14:29.585 --> 14:33.453
Stainless steel submariner,
waterproof to up to 300 meters.

14:33.622 --> 14:35.317
And look, it winds itself.

14:39.895 --> 14:43.092
Put it on your right arm, it'll run forever.

14:48.571 --> 14:50.471
Oh, good thinking.

14:50.639 --> 14:52.573
Oh, hey, look, what else I got?

14:52.741 --> 14:55.767
Genuine porcelain veneer.

14:56.845 --> 14:59.177
From an English-speaking dentist.

15:00.215 --> 15:03.673
"From an English-speaking dentist."

15:05.754 --> 15:07.153
Hey, Jake. I need a favor.

15:07.323 --> 15:09.382
Sorry, I can't say bad things
about Grandma.

15:10.593 --> 15:14.359
Okay. What did she buy you?
New guitar? Mini bike?

15:15.030 --> 15:16.054
Pizza.

15:17.900 --> 15:19.731
You sold me out for a pizza?

15:20.235 --> 15:23.068
Not just a pizza, a meat lovers pizza.

15:29.878 --> 15:35.373
&lt;i>M is for the misery she caused me&lt;/i>

15:36.518 --> 15:40.852
&lt;i>O is for the other things she did&lt;/i>

15:42.191 --> 15:48.187
&lt;i>T is for the traitor who's my brother&lt;/i>

15:48.897 --> 15:55.097
&lt;i>H is for the hump who is his kid&lt;/i>

15:56.271 --> 15:57.898
No, it's true.

15:58.073 --> 16:00.803
They can bleach anything these days.

16:00.976 --> 16:02.102
Really?

16:02.277 --> 16:03.744
It's gotta burn like hell.

16:03.912 --> 16:06.346
Like a lit cigar.

16:07.282 --> 16:08.408
But it's worth it.

16:08.584 --> 16:11.246
Curb appeal isn't just for the front door.

16:11.787 --> 16:16.850
&lt;i>E is for extremely frightening girl talk&lt;/i>

16:17.993 --> 16:19.961
- Oh, hey, honey.
- How was shopping?

16:20.129 --> 16:21.721
Mom, pick up any new souls?

16:24.433 --> 16:26.060
Charlie, that's uncalled for.

16:26.502 --> 16:28.367
It's okay, Chelsea.

16:28.537 --> 16:29.697
He can't help himself.

16:30.139 --> 16:31.163
Yes, he can.

16:31.340 --> 16:33.900
There's no excuse
for speaking to your mother that way.

16:34.710 --> 16:36.575
You don't know that.

16:37.546 --> 16:39.571
Evelyn, thank you for a wonderful day.

16:39.748 --> 16:43.878
Pleasure was mine.
It's nice to be appreciated for a change.

16:44.053 --> 16:45.884
- We on for yoga tomorrow?
- Can't wait.

16:47.723 --> 16:50.783
Oh, and, of course, you and Charlie
are coming for dinner on Saturday.

16:50.959 --> 16:53.018
- We wouldn't miss it.
- Um, um...

16:53.195 --> 16:54.492
Actually...

16:54.663 --> 16:57.097
...Chels, we have plans on Saturday,
remember?

16:57.266 --> 17:01.828
- What plans?
- Oh, for God sake, can't you just play along?

17:03.672 --> 17:07.005
- We'll be there.
- Wonderful. Ta-ta.

17:09.144 --> 17:12.807
- You proud of yourself?
- Not really, I lost that one.

17:15.584 --> 17:20.044
&lt;i>R is for the rifle in my mouth&lt;/i>

17:22.891 --> 17:28.625
&lt;i>Put them all together they spell "mother"&lt;/i>

17:29.331 --> 17:34.826
&lt;i>A word that's only half of how I feel&lt;/i>

17:44.947 --> 17:46.278
Hello.

17:46.749 --> 17:49.149
I am Alan Cousteau.

17:51.386 --> 17:53.877
I left the Calypso...

17:54.623 --> 17:57.592
...at 0500 hours...

17:57.760 --> 18:01.992
...and have descended
to a depth of 60 fathoms.

18:02.164 --> 18:07.124
And yet my Rolex
is keeping perfect time.

18:09.571 --> 18:10.629
Oh, look...

18:10.806 --> 18:13.104
...there goes a giant squid.

18:13.575 --> 18:15.440
Alan?

18:19.815 --> 18:21.305
Yes?

18:22.050 --> 18:23.074
What are you doing?

18:24.686 --> 18:26.017
Um...

18:27.790 --> 18:29.781
I got no good answer.

18:31.794 --> 18:34.024
It's Saturday night, and I'm all alone.

18:34.696 --> 18:38.496
Do you know where Charlie is?
We're supposed to be at your mother's at 7.

18:39.034 --> 18:41.832
Oh. You are cutting it close.

18:43.906 --> 18:44.930
Have you seen him?

18:45.107 --> 18:47.507
Not for a
couple hours. Have you tried his cell?

18:47.676 --> 18:49.837
I did, there's no answer.
I'm getting worried.

18:51.213 --> 18:53.613
CHARLIE: Chelsea, I'm home.
- Thank goodness.

18:55.584 --> 18:58.382
I return to the deep.

18:59.688 --> 19:01.087
Where have you been?

19:01.256 --> 19:03.224
Picking up a little surprise for you.

19:03.392 --> 19:05.223
Come on in.

19:06.628 --> 19:11.531
- Mom?
- Hello, sweetie. Oh. Ooh.

19:11.700 --> 19:14.100
Feels like you gave up
on the Jenny Craig, huh?

19:16.471 --> 19:19.497
- What are you doing here?
- I flew her in from Illinois.

19:19.675 --> 19:21.734
First class, very swanky.

19:21.910 --> 19:25.744
Of course, I had some rich Jew lawyer
chewing my ear off the whole way.

19:27.049 --> 19:28.414
Tell her about the food.

19:28.584 --> 19:30.916
Oh, the food was terrific...

19:31.086 --> 19:34.613
...but the flight attendant
was a colored homo.

19:36.058 --> 19:39.289
Really, I'm glad they make them pick up
the dinner rolls with tongs...

19:39.461 --> 19:41.395
...because I can't risk the AIDS.

19:44.233 --> 19:46.793
I hope you didn't fill up.
We're going for dinner.

19:46.969 --> 19:49.369
Oh, how nice.

19:49.538 --> 19:51.130
Now, be honest with me, Charlie.

19:51.306 --> 19:55.970
You're so dark and handsome,
you gotta have some dago in you, right?

19:59.214 --> 20:01.978
God, I love your mom.

20:08.690 --> 20:11.682
That was the worst dinner of my life.

20:12.394 --> 20:15.295
Really? I thought the two moms hit it off.

20:15.864 --> 20:18.298
Kind of country mouse, city mouse.

20:18.800 --> 20:23.100
I especially liked the part
when country mouse kicked off her shoes...

20:23.272 --> 20:26.935
...put her big yellow bunions up
on city mouse's mahogany coffee table...

20:27.709 --> 20:31.770
...and asked her how she liked
having a commie Arab for a president.

20:33.515 --> 20:35.107
You've made your point, Charlie.

20:35.284 --> 20:38.310
Point? Whatever do you mean?

20:38.487 --> 20:41.217
You leave my mother alone,
and I'll leave yours alone.

20:41.390 --> 20:43.085
Well, gosh, I don't know.

20:43.258 --> 20:45.123
I've really taken a shine to your mom.

20:46.228 --> 20:49.356
She promised to teach me
how to chew tobacco and burn a cross.

20:50.165 --> 20:51.530
Do we have a deal or not?

20:52.034 --> 20:53.467
Deal. Come here.

20:53.635 --> 20:55.500
I'm not in the mood.

20:55.671 --> 20:56.968
All right.

20:57.139 --> 21:00.302
But don't be rubbing up against me
in the middle of the night.

21:00.609 --> 21:01.735
Don't worry, I won't.

21:02.444 --> 21:03.502
Good night.

21:03.679 --> 21:05.271
Good night.

21:13.755 --> 21:15.746
All right, I was bluffing.

21:17.893 --> 21:19.690
Feel free to rub.

21:19.928 --> 21:22.192
Rub yourself.

21:24.433 --> 21:25.457
Chels?

21:25.634 --> 21:27.158
What?

21:28.070 --> 21:31.062
Can you watch me so it's not weird?
